Description: Contribution-adjusted meta-analysis (CAMS) for
    treatment-by-subgroup interactions from subgroup-level aggregate data
    (Panaro, Röver & Friede, 2025, arXiv:2512.18785). The package constructs
    trial information fractions, rotates subgroup estimates into orthogonal
    overall and interaction series, and reconstructs contribution-adjusted
    interaction, subgroup, and combined-population effects. CAMS can be
    fitted using Bayesian or frequentist inference. Bayesian CAMS uses
    'bayesmeta' (DIRECT quadrature; binary subgroups); frequentist CAMS uses
    'metafor' (REML/ML). Difference of Averages (DA) and Average Difference
    (AD) are different constructions (Panaro, Röver & Friede, 2026); the
    SWADA shared-weight principle is included as context, not as an
    alternative CAMS model.
URL: https://arxiv.org/abs/2512.18785
